[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
OpenProject %%VERSION%% is installed at %%WWWDIR%%.

This is a native CloudBSD Rails port (www/gitlab rc.d/Gemfile
pattern plus CloudBSD JSON/rc.d/mdoc/doctor wrappers): Puma on
127.0.0.1:3000 and a separate good_job worker rc.d. nginx is
already the jail TLS reverse proxy (X-Forwarded-Proto https).
Docker, .deb, and linux_base are not used. BIM IFC converters
(Linux blobs), hocuspocus, and Appsignal are not enabled.

OpenProject cannot consume JSON. It reads environment variables
(DATABASE_URL, SECRET_KEY_BASE, OPENPROJECT_HOST__NAME,
OPENPROJECT_HTTPS, memcache). The file it actually uses is:

  %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/openproject.env

An optional JSON file under the same directory can generate
that env file (`openproject env`) if you want CloudBSD JSON
as the editor format. It is not read by OpenProject itself.

1. Copy the env sample and set secrets:

     cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/openproject.env.sample \
        %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/openproject.env
     # set SECRET_KEY_BASE once (openssl rand -hex 64) and keep it
     # set DATABASE_URL password
     chmod 0600 %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/openproject.env

   SECRET_KEY_BASE must be unique per install and persistent
   across upgrades. Do not regenerate it on every start.

2. PostgreSQL 16 or 17 (matching the port option):

     createuser -P openproject
     createdb -O openproject openproject

3. Enable memcached. Merge
   %%PREFIX%%/etc/nginx/openproject.conf.sample
   into the jail vhost (certbot already on track).

4. First-time schema:

     openproject migrate

5. Check and start Puma and the worker (two rc.d scripts):

     openproject doctor
     sysrc openproject_enable=YES
     sysrc openproject_worker_enable=YES
     service openproject start
     service openproject_worker start

Default login is admin / admin. Change it immediately.

Man pages: openproject(8), openproject.conf(5)
ENV file:  %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/openproject.env
EOM
}
]
